# Rover Metro (R6), 1990-1994.
#
# The October 1990 Rover Metro was the Metro re-engineered around the K-series
# engine and a Peugeot gearbox, with revised Hydragas suspension and a restyled
# front and rear on the same body shell. It was sold as the Rover 100 outside
# Britain; the 100 nameplate reached the home market only in 1994.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Austin_Metro
#
# Dimensions 3.406 x 1.565 x 1.359 m, wheelbase 2.250 m; the published Rover
# Metro / 100 dimension box. The track is wider than the Mk2's and the length
# 3 mm greater, so the hull and wheel positions are adjusted from the Mk2 master
# but the shell and wheelbase are shared.
#
# The three-door body is modelled, as for the Mk2: extra door divisions do not
# read at 128 px.
#
# Colours: Flame Red (BLVC 818), White Diamond (655), Silver Leaf metallic (421)
# and Zircon Blue metallic (471), all Rover UK offerings of 1990-94. The split is
# era-adjusted from the 1994-96 measured base towards red and white, which were
# markedly stronger on early-1990s registrations, and away from silver: red 6,
# white 4, silver 3, blue 3. Total 16. Provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 130 km/h, one step above the Mk2 for the K-series and five-speed gearbox.
# Comfort 60/270, on the line 180 + 1.5 x 60, a step above the Mk2's 50/255 for the
# revised Hydragas and the quieter K-series, and one step below the Corsa B's
# 65/280. Classes 0,1,2.
#
# Dates are road presence, not production: May 1990 intro, retires staggered
# 2001-2004 on an eleven- to fourteen-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/rover-metro.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/rover-metro.dae (33 objects). Variant of the Metro Mk2 shell;
# references: citycars/references/rover-metro/ (gitignored; six photographs from
# Wikimedia Commons, CC BY 2.0 and CC BY-SA 4.0).
#
# Accepted low-poly deviations, recorded rather than corrected: angular surfaces
# stand in for the photographed rounded corners, and the tail lamp clusters are
# the short units the photographs show, not the full-height units the brief
# guessed at. Stage B ran in connectivity mode because the hatch glass sits on the
# cabin, above the hull's top face.

obj=citycar
name=RoverMetro(FlameRed)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=6
intro_year=1990
intro_month=5
retire_year=2001
retire_month=6
speed=130
class=0,1,2
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=60
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=270

Image[E]=./images/rover-metro-red_E.0.0,-33,14
Image[SE]=./images/rover-metro-red_SE.0.0,-13,0
Image[S]=./images/rover-metro-red_S.0.0,0,0
